  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 140 AM CDT Fri Jul 10 2026\n\nIt isn't often that a building upper high pressure system causes\nour temperatures to cool, but that is what will happen over the\nweekend and into next week. The key is that the high doesn't build\nover TX/NM, but over the northern Great Plains leaving West Texas\nand eastern New Mexico under lower heights and increasing\nsoutheasterly flow. Cool, moist gulf air advects into the area\ndropping temps below normal next week with highs in the lower 90s\nto upper 80s. The moisture also causes rain chances to increase\nnext week with the highest PoPs in the higher elevations west of\nthe Pecos River. More widely scattered hit and miss afternoon \nshowers and thunderstorms are expected in the Permian Basin but\nhopefully everyone will see a little rain at least one day next\nweek. \n\nHennig",
